  "worked_solution": "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=-1$ and $k=-7,$ the vertex is $(-1,-7).$\n\n- Since $a=-3<0,$ the parabola opens downwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens downwards, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output. \n\nTherefore, the range is $(-\\infty ,-7].$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14250418/assets/21049fc3aa8d6e2b64c4fd5db723c00e5878473ad8b96f25271c46edc48ed3ea.png)",
